# Keep the build context small and the image reproducible.
#
# models/, corpus/ and index/ are bind-mounted at run time (see Makefile), so
# baking them into the image would duplicate gigabytes and make the image
# depend on whatever happened to be on the builder's disk.

# The whole corpus tree is bind-mounted at run time (see Makefile MOUNTS), so
# nothing under it belongs in the image.
#
# This previously read `corpus/raw/` plus a bare `*.zip`, and .dockerignore
# patterns DO NOT RECURSE: `*.zip` matches only top-level files, so the 1.8 GB
# Infonet archive at corpus/external/infonet.zip was copied in. That inflated
# the image from 1.55 GB to 5.41 GB and - far worse - would have had the image
# redistribute CC BY-NC-SA material, defeating the entire reason the corpus is
# fetched by manifest rather than committed.
models/
index/
corpus/
bench/traces/
bench/results/

.git/
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

tests/fixtures/
docs/assets/

# Recursive forms. Bare `*.ext` only matches the build-context root.
**/*.gguf
**/*.onnx
**/*.bin
**/*.safetensors
**/*.pdf
**/*.zip
**/*.mp4

.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
